{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
  "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KULEWICZ: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: For four decades, the Medicare Secondary Payer Act has been a coordination of benefits statute. It establishes that a group health plan must pay its benefits first during a 30-month coordination period when the plan and Medicare both cover an individual who must contend with end-stage renal disease. The plan must not take into account the Medicare entitlement or eligibility of an individual during that time or differentiate in the benefits that it provides between individuals with end-stage renal disease and other individuals covered by the plan on a basis that relates to that diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents fail to state a claim under the Medicare Secondary Payer Act. Because the alleged violations of the Medicare Secondary Payer Act are the express and only basis of their ERISA claims, Respondents also fail to state a claim under ERISA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the participant will be paying roughly $96 per treatment, but, if the Court grants the relief ultimately that DaVita seeks, that same individual will be paying 30 percent of -- according to the Pacific Health Coalition amicus brief, the dialysis charges range from $1,041 to $6,000 per treatment. So that same participant, instead of paying $96 per treatment, would be paying up to -- up to $1800 per treatment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why -- why does this not violate the statute from your point of view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, I'm somewhat baffled by this -- the statutory language."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KULEWICZ: Your Honor, if the Court were to affirm the Sixth Circuit and -- and it goes back and judgment is entered for what DaVita seeks here, which is the right to be paid its undiscounted charges, it would be disastrous for people who have end-stage renal disease and are -- are covered simply by plans because that would be the situation where right now they're paying 30 percent of 125 percent of the Medicare rate, which is -- which would be in the $90 range, $96 range. Paying 30 percent of the undiscounted charges could be up to $1800 per treatment, and that would very quickly exhaust their -- exhaust resources and --and reach their out-of-pocket maximum within the space of -- of two to three treatments here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Let me say it again if you didn't get it. Did you get it or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could ultimately lead to greater costs for the Medicare program and -- and potentially worse coverage or worse options for individuals with end-stage renal disease."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Differential treatment of outpatient renal dialysis is most certainly differential treatment of individuals with ESRD. Congress determined that, and it determined it because Congress understood in 1972 and in 1981 and thereafter that ESRD patients uniquely and utterly need outpatient dialysis for the rest of their lives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is that vulnerable?\nIs that illegal in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Who -- who are you going to compare it with?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kidney Care Partners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if you look, for example, not only at the -- the Kidney Care Partners' amicus brief but also the brief of former CMS Administrator Scully, he explains why that's the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Are you finished with --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner says, look, what they wanted was parity. They wanted parity between ESRD patients. They wanted them to have the same benefits whether you have ESRD or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it expressly touts the benefit of its ability to \"reduce dialysis procedures provided to ESRD patients\" by implementing our proprietary dialysis health plan language."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DaVita never tells you or never says either in the record or even up to today that it wants to come into the network. What it seeks is the right to be paid at its undiscounted charges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1641",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f7fd77b06ae5ea33ab8418039e48f105dfdf2b10ab0898793d891003f71fd506",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f7fd77b06ae5-0004-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
